# Conventional Commit Message Template for mtk-gui
#
# Format:
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   [optional body]
#
#   [optional footer(s)]
#
# ---------------------- type choices ----------------------
#   feat:     new feature (e.g. new UI page, new test step type)
#   fix:      bug fix
#   docs:     documentation only changes
#   style:    formatting, missing semicolons, no logic change
#   refactor: code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     performance improvement (e.g. waveform rendering cache)
#   test:     adding or correcting test scripts
#   chore:    build, packaging, git, tooling, CI changes
#
# ---------------------- scope (optional) ------------------
#   Suggested scopes: workflow, console, equipment, config,
#   virtual, login, theme, build, docs
#
# ---------------------- subject rules ---------------------
#   - imperative mood: "add" not "added" / "adds"
#   - max 50 characters, no trailing period
#   - first letter lowercase after the prefix
#
# ---------------------- body (optional) -------------------
#   - wrap lines at 72 characters
#   - explain WHAT changed and WHY, not HOW
#
# ---------------------- footer (optional) -----------------
#   - BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the breaking change>
#   - Refs: <issue or ticket id>
#
# Examples:
#   feat(workflow): add Long Run interval locking rule
#   fix(console): track real connection state for fctconn steps
#   chore(build): package config folder into Windows exe
